 ### Polygon-Based Volume Rendering
-A direct volume rendering system based on generalized software scan conversion of polygons rather than ray-casting, projection, or splatting of cells [S7, unofficial]. It decomposes any cell type into a set of bounding polygons to render semi-transparent regions of space between polygons as well as opaque surfaces [S7, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its siblings by handling overlapping cells in multi-grid data sets correctly and working on arbitrary polygons without re-gridding [S7, unofficial]. Choose it for complex, irregular, or decimated volumes where traditional cell projection fails.
